An Azure Environment Health Score provides an overall assessment of cloud health by combining multiple operational metrics into a single evaluation.

Evaluation areas include:

* Security posture
* Resource availability
* Compliance status
* Backup health
* Monitoring effectiveness
* Cost efficiency
* Documentation quality

# Real-Life Example:
For example, an environment may achieve a health score of 92% after demonstrating strong governance, reliable monitoring, and excellent operational practices.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is organizations comparing operational maturity across multiple Azure subscriptions.

Health scoring simplifies executive reporting and operational planning.
